    "summary": "Lakeland ’82 delivers a blazing second set with thunderous Not Fade Away and pristine sound",
    "review": "The Dead hit their stride at the Lakeland Civic Center on September 12, 1982. The first set rolls smoothly through classics like \"Alabama Getaway\" and a funk‑laden \"West L.A.\", but it’s the second set that truly lifts off – a seamless cascade from \"Man Smart, Woman Smarter\" into a soaring \"Playing in the Band\", tight drums, and an exhilarating ride through \"Drums → Space → The Wheel\". The band locks in for a blistering \"Not Fade Away\" closer that bursts with Brent’s bright B‑3 stabs, then drifts into a heartfelt \"Morning Dew\" before winding down with a sweet \"Sugar Magnolia\". Jerry’s voice is expressive and his guitar on “Might As Well” sings, even if he sounds a touch weary at times; Phil’s bass stays present despite being low in the mix, while Brent adds jazzy, experimental flair that occasionally rides high over the band. Mickey and Bill’s interplay is crisp and jazz‑inflected, giving the jams an extra swing. All told, this show captures the 1982 Dead at a creative peak – energetic, tight, and brimming with memorable moments.",
